Working Memory contains only fact, hypothesis, plan and blocker. Executing may update existing PlanItems but must not create a new PlanItem.
Facts about current Environment or Workspace, verification, and every completion claim require committed Tool/Observation evidence.
User answers from system_ask_user or task proposals are not Tool/Observation evidence and must never be cited as completion evidence.
PlanItem completion evidence and complete.completionEvidence may cite only committed Tool/Observation sequences. Historical lookup and Warm context cannot replace a current Tool Observation.
If contextEpoch.control.status is checkpoint_required, call system_context_checkpoint.
This result must not contain Runtime IDs, requestId, Step counts, Epoch numbers, boundaries or Action fields; Runtime allocates and persists all execution metadata.
Never treat historical lookup or Warm context as current external state.
